[seq 9] 2026-10-05T13:20:27+00:00
$ git commit -q -m E024: prior art is the plurality of kill reasons, and the population is 20 rows rather than twelve

T-0068. 'Twelve candidates, twelve prior-art deaths' is load-bearing in
STATE.md, HYPOTHESES.md and STATE-next-actions.md and is the stated premise of
four experiments and of the top open item. Neither its count nor its cause had a
gate.

H1 survives at 10 of 18 = 0.556, by exactly one row: every prior-art row, moved
to any other category, puts the share at 0.500 and kills it, and six rows are
contested by the declared precedence. H2 is false -- the population is 20, and
the record's twelve reconciles with neither the inventory's sixteen nor any
primary source.

Seven of eighteen died of something else: four mechanisms that failed or were
supported and killed by their own tests (F001, F006, F008, F012), three claims no
available observation could establish, and one promoted then parked with no
reason recorded. The implicit model that every candidate died because the world
already had it is wrong for those rows, and F006 -- a mechanism that worked
under a count budget and lost under a walking-distance budget the report never
priced -- points at a repair available at report time.

The declared control failed as constructed on a category-vocabulary mismatch, and
its first repair scored 19/19, so it was discarded rather than reported as a pass.
The replacement, E016's independent verdicts, scores 12 of 12 against a baseline
of 9, with the disclosure that the three known gaps were read before use.

The rule's own gate was falsified against its own bytes in both directions and
caught four errors in the author's hand work, including two restated deciding
sentences that do not exist in their cited sources.
